# Benchmark: count the primes below ten million with `primes` from
# examples/sieve.chasm. Run as `chasm run examples/sieve.chasm bench/sieve.chasm`.
# Prints the checksum, then the nanoseconds the work took.

: main ( -- )
  now :> t0
  10000000 primes array.len :> count
  now t0 i64.sub :> ns
  count i32.to-str print " " print ns i64.to-str println ;
